  "intro": "The Arabic alphabet with the sound of every letter, its shapes, how to read without vowel marks, and a key to the symbols in the pronunciations.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "How the Arabic alphabet works",
      "text": [
        "Arabic is written from right to left in an alphabet of 28 letters, all consonants. ا, و and ي also stand for the long vowels aa, uu and ii.",
        "The script is joined, like handwriting: most letters connect to the next one and change shape depending on where they fall in a word. Six letters — ا د ذ ر ز و — never join to the letter after them, which leaves a small gap."
      ]
    },
